  \includegraphics[width=\columnwidth]{fig_psd_scaleup.pdf}
  \caption{Power spectral density slope $\alpha$ of the 2D-embedded
           prime gap surface at $N=10^5$ and $N=10^6$. The observed
           $\alpha \approx 0$ (near-white noise) definitively
           excludes the $1/f$ spectrum ($\alpha = -1$) reported by
           Wolf~\cite{WOLF-1997} for the 1D prime gap sequence.
           The deviation from $1/f$ increases with $N$
           ($z = 37.8 \to 129.1$).}
  \label{fig:psd-scaleup}
