           $|\Delta D_2| = 0.003$) at all scales, while M\"obius
           $\mu^-$ and Beatty $\varphi$ fluctuate. Square-free
           numbers remain within the threshold. Bottom: power-law
           fit $|\Delta D_2| \propto N^{-\gamma}$ for primes
           ($\gamma \approx 0.107$).}
  \label{fig:convergence}
\end{figure}



Square-free numbers, the negative control, exhibit
$\Delta D_2$ consistent with zero at all scales tested,
confirming that the metrological fingerprint does not produce
false positives for sequences lacking arithmetic correlation
structure.

